        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "d85b3a2c-6c9f-3332-8c58-598a11dfbfeb",
                "word": "javelle",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "181e4ab0-03f7-4afd-8a7b-6118c01627af",
                        "entry_id": "d85b3a2c-6c9f-3332-8c58-598a11dfbfeb",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "javelles"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bd933ab2-49f8-3549-8281-1972cebc8bfc",
                        "entry_id": "d85b3a2c-6c9f-3332-8c58-598a11dfbfeb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Plusieurs brassées de blés, de seigle, d’avoine fauchées, qui demeurent à sécher sur le sol avant d’en faire des gerbes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "de0ac6fc-05fa-3d82-b7b4-1ac6b3418b66",
                        "entry_id": "d85b3a2c-6c9f-3332-8c58-598a11dfbfeb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Des hommes coupent le blé avec des faucilles en tout semblables à celles dont se servent nos agriculteurs ; à mesure que les épis tombent, on les ramasse pour les lier en javelles. — (Maxime Du Camp, Le Nil : Égypte et Nubie, 1854)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c3179a35-71b9-38dd-ae60-18c02520ddb2",
                        "entry_id": "d85b3a2c-6c9f-3332-8c58-598a11dfbfeb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "À chaque coup, je fermais les yeux, tout étourdi ; puis, quand je me décidais à les ouvrir, je voyais la plaine grande et nue, les chiens courant, furetant dans les brins d’herbe, dans les javelles, tournant sur eux-mêmes comme des fous. — (Alphonse Daudet, « Les émotions d’un perdreau rouge », dans Contes du lundi, 1873, Fasquelle, collection Le Livre de Poche, 1974, page 221)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "aacf9946-fc8e-3c86-b5b7-9873b2bebc87",
                        "entry_id": "d85b3a2c-6c9f-3332-8c58-598a11dfbfeb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Elle revenait des fermes éparpillées autour du petit château, rapportant son butin de nouvelles et des javelles d’avoine verte, des coquelicots et des nielles, les premières digitales des ravins pierreux. — (Sidonie-Gabrielle Colette, La Maison de Claudine, Hachette, 1922, coll. Livre de Poche, 1960, page 110)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a19dacea-5bf7-3763-be10-3db0e4c9040c",
                        "entry_id": "d85b3a2c-6c9f-3332-8c58-598a11dfbfeb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Les Belges sont là, ils travaillent depuis les premières lueurs de l’aube. Ils sont en ligne et balancent leur faux d’un mouvement régulier et assuré. Derrière eux, les botteleurs lient des gerbes et les dressent en javelles. Tous les gestes, toutes les attitudes sont bien rythmées comme les figures d’un ballet. — (Édouard Bled, J’avais un an en 1900, Fayard, 1987, Le Livre de Poche, page 140)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "aab0b62f-1cb4-3dc1-885c-f29aa77c4a13",
                        "entry_id": "d85b3a2c-6c9f-3332-8c58-598a11dfbfeb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Á La Horgne, un arpent fauché et lié rapportait deux doubles décalitres au faucheur et un à la femme qui faisait les javelles. — (Jacques Lambert, Campagnes et paysans des Ardennes : 1830-1914, Charleville-Mézières : éditions Terres ardennaises, 1988, p. 224)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d356a1a6-e3c7-37ae-a205-23c313d5bd23",
                        "entry_id": "d85b3a2c-6c9f-3332-8c58-598a11dfbfeb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "En ouvrant l’entaille dans les champs de blé, je formais une croix avec la première javelle. — (Émile Guillaumin, La Vie d’un simple, Éditions Le livre de poche, 1980, p. 260)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e913595d-17c6-32b6-8d69-d0994f454b21",
                        "entry_id": "d85b3a2c-6c9f-3332-8c58-598a11dfbfeb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Petits faisceaux de sarment."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "00fb9bb4-2f5e-4369-9543-826c361b7b45",
                                "sense_id": "e913595d-17c6-32b6-8d69-d0994f454b21",
                                "text": "Mettez une javelle au feu."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e9311c13-449c-37bd-8ff2-6307b369e120",
                        "entry_id": "d85b3a2c-6c9f-3332-8c58-598a11dfbfeb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Tas de sel tiré des marais salants."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "740f9f97-d728-314a-8a58-c1762ce01582",
                        "entry_id": "d85b3a2c-6c9f-3332-8c58-598a11dfbfeb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Paquet de huit morues séchées."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cdb9c630-7fca-3cc7-a8d3-c364ea88b282",
                        "entry_id": "d85b3a2c-6c9f-3332-8c58-598a11dfbfeb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Tonneau tombé en javelle : Tonneau dont les douves se séparent du fond."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6ce8ce91-e390-464b-95f3-06a927249cd6",
                        "source_entry_id": "d85b3a2c-6c9f-3332-8c58-598a11dfbfeb",
                        "target_lang_word": "sheaf",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sheaf",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9c1a1299-dee3-3f3d-b331-745f517d6359",
                                        "entry_id": "db9c7c80-4816-3a89-b802-5ea699b64991",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A quantity of the stalks and ears of wheat, rye, or other grain, bound together; a bundle of grain or straw."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74dfcc37-14b3-4c82-8781-f7fcb1a6670d",
                                                "sense_id": "9c1a1299-dee3-3f3d-b331-745f517d6359",
                                                "text": "O, let me teach you how to knit again / This scattered corn into one mutual sheaf, / These broken limbs again into one body."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6aa1fc3-4747-4970-bb1c-f313b111d335",
                                                "sense_id": "9c1a1299-dee3-3f3d-b331-745f517d6359",
                                                "text": "Ev’n while the Reaper fills his greedy hands, / And binds the golden Sheafs in brittle bands"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2bf4dfa3-5cf1-387c-9f71-3ca42629dbfb",
                                        "entry_id": "db9c7c80-4816-3a89-b802-5ea699b64991",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any collection of things bound together."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "69be78af-8da7-4e78-83f7-ba3e88d5578f",
                                                "sense_id": "2bf4dfa3-5cf1-387c-9f71-3ca42629dbfb",
                                                "text": "a sheaf of paper"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5d9363f-4950-4e5e-bf8c-d5d8ef384cc9",
                                                "sense_id": "2bf4dfa3-5cf1-387c-9f71-3ca42629dbfb",
                                                "text": "Together the two men march up the aisle and mount the dais, and while Muspole shakes hands with the chairman and his lady, the major draws a sheaf of notes from a briefcase and lays them on the table."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1ffda69e-3bd7-34aa-9ebd-c7d84f8ca67c",
                                        "entry_id": "db9c7c80-4816-3a89-b802-5ea699b64991",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bundle of arrows sufficient to fill a quiver, or the allowance of each archer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2559a4f4-95c7-4092-ac7b-7be98ee38bb3",
                                                "sense_id": "1ffda69e-3bd7-34aa-9ebd-c7d84f8ca67c",
                                                "text": "The sheaf of arrows shook, and rattled in the case."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "33c4fcdc-090d-31a6-bba5-5195bffc2462",
                                        "entry_id": "db9c7c80-4816-3a89-b802-5ea699b64991",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A quantity of arrows, usually twenty-four."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed67347e-1ef4-482e-903c-adf7b9cbaedd",
                                                "sense_id": "33c4fcdc-090d-31a6-bba5-5195bffc2462",
                                                "text": "Arrows were anciently made of reeds, afterwards of cornel wood, and occasionally of every species of wood: but according to Roger Ascham, ash was best; arrows were reckoned by sheaves, a sheaf consisted of twenty-four arrows."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "41ad753c-5831-347c-9038-930caa629000",
                                        "entry_id": "db9c7c80-4816-3a89-b802-5ea699b64991",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sheave."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9b039555-b429-3eaa-8b4c-277781ba90fe",
                                        "entry_id": "db9c7c80-4816-3a89-b802-5ea699b64991",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An abstract construct in topology that associates data to the open sets of a topological space (i.e. a presheaf) in such a way so as to make the local and global data compatible, generalizing the situation of functions, fiber bundles, manifold structure, etc. on a topological space. Formally, a presheaf ℱ whose sections are, in a technical sense, uniquely determined by their restrictions onto smaller sets: that is, given an open cover U_i of U:",
                                            "If two sections over U agree under restriction to every U_i, then the sections are the same."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b627f59b-f0f9-3cff-9a21-1f98b9ff0f09",
                                        "entry_id": "db9c7c80-4816-3a89-b802-5ea699b64991",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An abstract construct in topology that associates data to the open sets of a topological space (i.e. a presheaf) in such a way so as to make the local and global data compatible, generalizing the situation of functions, fiber bundles, manifold structure, etc. on a topological space. Formally, a presheaf ℱ whose sections are, in a technical sense, uniquely determined by their restrictions onto smaller sets: that is, given an open cover U_i of U:",
                                            "Given a family of sections s_i∈ℱ(U_i) such that all pairs (s_i,s_j) agree under restriction to U_i∩U_j, there is a (unique) section s over U whose restriction to U_i is s_i."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "sheaf",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aa575e08-83fb-380c-9652-d79432b70687",
                                        "entry_id": "0ed5fc05-27a4-3544-b20e-b751307dd6ef",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To gather and bind into a sheaf; to make into sheaves"
                                        ],
